The mad king and his testerone-obsessed secretary of WAR plan to livestream the execution by firing squad of former Army psychiatrist Nidal Hasan, who killed 13 people at Fort Hood in 2009. 
No one needs to defend Hasan's crimes to say that public execution is barbaric and wrong. Few countries carry out public executions, among them Afghanistan and Iran, according to Amnesty International. NO modern democracies have public executions. 

Historian Timothy Snyder listed a number of reasons why such a spectacle is wrong, including: 
"It is wrong politically. To livestream an execution will not deter terrorism. It will invite terrorism, as Mr. Hegseth no doubt understands. The deeper political consequence, however, is domestic. The basis of politics in the Trump regime is sado-populism. Rather than offer policy that benefits Americans, Trump uses the government to hurt some, and offer their pain as a spectacle to everyone else. To livestream a public execution is to take that politics to its logical extreme. The federal government would be instructing us to observe, and thus participate in, a public killing. This invitation to us is a major step towards seeing politics only as the pain of other."

Thank you to our marshals from @indivisiblelancastertogether 

To join our vigil, email boldactionworks@gmail.com

